    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: an owner may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation` = title + ' ' + lastName, or just lastName when no title is given.\n\nChanges, following the existing generated-DTO + MapStruct + OfficeFloor patterns:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (string enum MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the writable `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are code-generated from this spec, so both fields flow through automatically.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` column mapping with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` expression: `title` blank/null \u2192 `lastName`, else `title + \" \" + lastName`. MapStruct auto-maps the input `title` (enum \u21c4 String) both ways with no extra config.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column (tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is required; the other dialects were updated for consistency).\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests` passes and all 56 existing tests remain green.",
